  "names": {
    "order": "given family",
    "conventions": "Ewe and Mina children get a day name for the day of the week they were born: Kossi or Kossiwa (Sunday), Kodjo or Adjoa (Monday), Komlan or Abla (Tuesday), Kokou or Akouvi (Wednesday), Yao or Yawa (Thursday), Koffi or Afi (Friday), Komi or Ama (Saturday). Many also carry a name with Mawu (God), like Mawuli or Mawuena, or Sena and Elom, and a French Christian first name. Family names come from the father; old coastal families of Aného and Lomé carry Afro-Brazilian or English names like d'Almeida, de Souza, Lawson and Johnson.",
